# tests/play.script - a game by keys (make test), each step after the program says it is
# ready for it (run816.py's "wait": the console lines the port prints), not at fixed
# seconds: a slower or faster start, Horizon or SDK changes the time things take, not what
# happens. The title; a game; the digger up the middle column through its five emeralds
# (125 points); then left alone until the nobbins have taken its three lives; game over,
# the initials HZD (125 is a high score); the title with the new high score; F8 saves the
# game's recording (HZD125.DRF, check.sh plays it back); Esc. No pictures: those are of a
# recorded game at game frames (tests/frames.sh).
0 wait digger: title
+1000 key enter 100
+0 wait digger: play
+500 key up 4500
+0 wait digger: dead
+0 wait digger: play
+0 wait digger: dead
+0 wait digger: play
+0 wait digger: dead
+0 wait digger: initials
+500 HZD
+0 wait digger: title
+1500 key f8 100
+0 wait digger: title
+1500 key esc 100
